# promise: #578
# An extension makes a normal window on about:blank and goes on using the id windows.create gave it back, as
# BrowserSkill's Agent Window does (#578). Cra never shows Chrome's normal windows: their pages become Cra tabs
# and the window closes. It closed a window with nothing in it too, so the extension's id named no window:
# windows.get and tabs.create on it failed and windows.getAll never listed it (engine -27 answered
# get-missing-listed-false-tab-error-query-0-remove-error-removed-true, onRemoved from Cra's own close). Now a
# window with only a blank page stays, unseen, as on the CEF bridge, and works as in Chrome until the extension
# closes it. A normal window on a page
# still becomes a Cra tab (adopted-closed, and `back` reads it as the selected tab).
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}
extension ${FIXTURES}/NormalWindowExtension
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=normal-window
expect-log GET /page\.html\?n=normal-window-
expect-log GET /page\.html\?n=in-window
expect-log GET /page\.html\?n=normal-window-get-ok-listed-true-tab-ok-query-2-remove-ok-removed-true-adopted-closed
cra://debug?back=adopted
expect-log back adopted: selected=.*page\.html\?n=adopted
reject-log fault:
